#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:50
msgid "Things are hung on walls in the 3D view: drag an item onto a wall. Buying a wall-only item from the floor plan switches to 3D for you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:51
msgid "In the 3D view, Q and E turn the view a quarter at a time and W/A/S/D move it. Scroll to zoom, left-drag empty floor to pan, middle-drag to orbit freely, middle-click to recenter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:52
msgid "The Walls button (or Home/End) switches between walls Up, Cutaway and Down. Cutaway lowers only the walls in front of where you are looking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:53
msgid "Double-click a box that has an apartment inside to step into it. Back takes you out one level; Map shows every apartment and jumps to any of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:54
msgid "Press R to rotate a piece — it cycles through all 4 facings, including a true 180° flip."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:55
msgid "Click a foldable piece (like a sofa bed) to fold or unfold it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:56
msgid "The Builder tab (next to Furniture) adds walls, columns, windows, doors, and paints floor kinds like balcony or bathroom."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:57
msgid "The dot in a piece's corner shows how easily it moves: green moves freely, yellow can move but makes the tenant less comfortable, red keeps one position all day unless it is on a rail. On larger pieces, one to three feathers beside the dot say the same thing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:58
msgid "The bar at the bottom is the goal: every need listed there has to be ticked."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:59
msgid "A piece with a heart after its name is a keepsake: it can be moved but never sold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:60
msgid "Furniture can move between an apartment and the boxes in it: drag a piece onto a box, or, from inside a box, onto the Back button. You go with it, and it is on your pointer ready to put down. Hold Shift as you let go to send it without going: it waits under Owned in that apartment's catalogue, free to place. Keepsakes stay where they are."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:61
msgid "Build has a Glass Wall beside the ordinary Wall: a real wall you can't put things or look through, but daylight passes it. Good for a guest room that would otherwise be dark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:62
msgid "Reeded glass and curtains hide what is behind them without darkening the room: they stop a line of sight and split a room into zones, but daylight passes. A curtain only does so while it is drawn (click it to draw it or pull it back)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:63
msgid "A caged bird needs daylight, and it sings: a bed within half a metre of it is no place to sleep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:64
msgid "You can also buy for another apartment: pick a piece in the catalogue and click it down on a box (or on Back). It is paid for from the budget of the apartment you are in and delivered to the other one, for a lodger whose own budget won't stretch."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:65
msgid "Rentals in the furniture catalogue are boxed apartments: placing one pays you its rent, in exchange for the floor it takes up. Removing it means paying the rent back. Double-click a box to look inside."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:66
msgid "Ctrl+%s undoes your last action; Ctrl+Shift+%s redoes it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:70
msgid "Press T to switch between the Floor Plan and 3D view."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:71
msgid "Press 1-9 to jump straight to a moment (Day, Night, ...) without clicking its tab."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/HowToPlay.gd:72
msgid "Press Up or Down to step to the floor above or below, Left or Right for the previous or next moment. On the floor plan W/S and A/D do the same."
msgstr ""

